{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's own claim measures the excess against the solo-rider optimal (11.5 km), but this is a RYDE_POOL trip. Under POL-RD-12 the baseline for POL-RD-01 is the matched-itinerary optimal recorded in trip_record.optimal_distance_km, which is 16.0 km, not the solo figure of 11.5 km. The rider has cited the wrong field and the claim fails on that ground alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02836"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The governing distance is the GPS trace figure of 16.96 km, not the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km of 17.0 km, because POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing field. Against the matched-itinerary optimal of 16.0 km the excess is 0.96 km, which is 6.00% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests must pass: the excess must exceed 20% of optimal AND exceed 0.8 km. The percentage test fails decisively at 6.00%, so no deviation is established.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02836", "EV-TRIP-02836"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The derived deviation block on the trace itself records status 'no deviation', with excess_km 0.96 and excess_pct 6.00 against the 16.0 km optimal. The trace is COMPLETE, 100.0% coverage, 133 fixes at a 10 s interval with zero gaps and a maximum gap of 0 s, so there is no POL-RD-07 impairment and no basis to look for independent corroboration. The measurement is clean and it is below threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02836"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's explanation is that the co-rider pickup is part of the pooled itinerary, and the trip record corroborates it: vehicle_type is RYDE_POOL and optimal_route_source records a 'matched pooled itinerary with one co-rider'. Distance attributable to collecting a co-rider on a platform-matched pooled itinerary is never a deviation under POL-RD-12 and is excluded from excess before POL-RD-01 is applied. The 0.96 km residual is exactly that kind of itinerary distance.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02836"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.optimal_route_source",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's arithmetic is also wrong on its own terms. The rider says the app matched 16.0 km but 'we drove 16.96 km' and then complains of a $23.51 fare. The fare breakdown shows the distance charge was computed on 17.0 km at $0.75/km = $12.75, plus $6.16 time charge, $3.80 base and $0.80 platform fee, totalling $23.51. The rider was billed for the pooled itinerary, not for a solo route, and the fare reconciles to the ledger with zero ERP lines.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02836"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No exculpatory clause is needed because no deviation is established, but the record is also free of any billing-integrity defect: erp_gantries is empty, tolls_erp is 0.0, airport_surcharge is 0.0, and the fare ledger reconciles to total_charged of $23.51. There is no phantom gantry and no wrongly applied surcharge to refund under POL-RD-09(4).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02836"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's profile does not assist the claim. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the POL-RD-08 corroboration uplift for a serial claimant (4 or more claims with 1 or fewer substantiated) is not engaged. The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and has not discharged it: the excess measured from the unimpaired trace does not meet the POL-RD-01 threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02836", "EV-GPS-02836"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's profile is clean for the POL-RD-06 test: deviation_flags_90d is 1, well below the 3-flag threshold, and 1/173 completed_trips_90d is 0.006, far below the 0.05 ratio. No repeat-deviation pattern is established, and no conduct referral is warranted. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and is not the trailing-90-day figure POL-RD-06 asks for.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02836"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The traffic advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-02836-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so no advisory covers the Blk 231 Serangoon Ave 3 corridor in this window. Neither party has cited it as an exculpatory ground, so POL-RD-13(1) applies: the absence is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction, and it does not trigger POL-RD-10(5). It is cited here only to record that no external traffic cause is on file and none is needed, because the deviation fails at the threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02836-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "admissibility.status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log is empty: message_count 0, no messages, not truncated. There is therefore no rider instruction in the chat log that could exonerate any distance under POL-RD-04, and equally no rider instruction that the trace failed to corroborate under POL-RD-14. The record is silent on both sides, and the case is decided on the trace and the matched-itinerary baseline alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02836"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-14"],
      "relies_on": "payload.message_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's claim that the driver 'picked up someone else' is not a deviation at all on this product. The trip record shows vehicle_type RYDE_POOL and the routing engine matched a pooled itinerary with one co-rider at booking time. A pooled trip is longer than any single rider's solo optimal by construction, which is precisely why POL-RD-12 sets the matched-itinerary figure as the baseline. The rider's $1.50 contested amount is the difference between the solo and pooled optimals, and the policy does not refund it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02836", "EV-FARE-02836"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.vehicle_type",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

